 - Writes require the `contributor` or `manager` role in the project. Users who can read but not write get 403.
 - Contributors may only modify tasks assigned to themselves, and may not reassign tasks. Managers may modify any task.
 - Only managers may delete tasks.
+- Moving a task is a manager-only action on its current project (like delete), and the actor must be able to write to the target project (contributor or manager there; else 404/403/409 as for writes). The task keeps its ID, title, status and assignee. If the assignee is not a contributor or manager of the target project, the move is 400 and nothing changes. Moving to the project the task is already in → 400.
 - Archived projects reject all writes with 409 (reads still work).
 - A task ID that does not belong to the project in the path → 404.
 
